---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { startingPrice } from '../data/services';

/* WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS.
   These are the terms for USING THIS WEBSITE — not for an engagement. Client
   work is governed by a signed agreement, and this page says so rather than
   trying to be one.

   THE LOAD-BEARING PART IS THE TOOLS DISCLAIMER. Nine tools on this site do
   real arithmetic on numbers a visitor types, and the free check prints a
   figure about their business. Every one of them is honest about being their
   own inputs through printed arithmetic — but somebody could still make a
   decision on one and then be unhappy. Saying plainly that these are
   calculators rather than advice is the whole point of the page.

   THE PRICE IS READ FROM THE DATA, never typed. startingPrice carries its own
   qualifier in the same object so no surface can show one without the other
   (D5 as amended). */

const UPDATED = '29 August 2026';
---
<MarketingLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms for using this website and the tools on it. Client work is governed by a signed agreement, not by this page."
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-line">
    <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <p class="mono-label">Terms of use</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        Using this site.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        For the website and the tools on it. Last updated {UPDATED}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="space-y-10 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">

      <div class="panel panel--flat rounded-lg p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">This page is not your contract</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If I build something for you, that work is governed by an agreement we both sign, which
          says what I owe you and what you own. <strong class="text-ink">Nothing on this page
          changes anything in that agreement</strong>, and where the two ever disagreed, the signed
          agreement would win.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Who runs this site</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Ian David Provencher, doing business as AppliedIQ Solutions — a sole proprietorship in
          New Bern, North Carolina. Using this site means you accept what is on this page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">The tools are calculators, not advice</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Every tool here works out an answer from numbers <em>you</em> type, using arithmetic it
          prints beside the result. None of them uses a model, a forecast, a benchmark or an
          industry average, and none of them suggests a rate, a target, a par or an interval —
          those are the decisions you are paid to make.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-ink">They are provided as they are, for information.</strong> They are
          not financial, legal, tax, accounting or employment advice, and a figure one of them
          prints is not a recommendation to do anything. Check anything that matters before you act
          on it. Where a tool cannot work something out, it says so rather than printing a plausible
          number — but that is a design principle, not a guarantee against every mistake.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Nothing you type into a tool is sent anywhere, stored by anyone, or seen by me. That means
          <strong class="text-ink">nothing is saved either</strong> — close the tab and it is gone.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">The free check</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          It multiplies out two numbers you give it and prints the working. It is the size of a
          problem, not a promise about what software would save you. What a build would actually
          change depends on what gets built.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Prices shown here</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          {startingPrice.line} {startingPrice.qualifier} Anything on this site about price is
          information, not an offer capable of being accepted.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">The demonstrations</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Every business, town, person and figure in the demonstrations is invented. They are not
          any real client's data and they are not a claim about any real business.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">What belongs to whom</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The design, text and code of this site are mine. You are welcome to read it, use the
          tools, and link to any page. You may not copy the site wholesale or pass it off as
          your own.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-ink">What I build for a client belongs to that client, outright</strong> —
          that is the entire point of how I work, and it is written into every agreement.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Meeting rooms</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          A meeting link I send is for you and expires after two weeks. Please do not pass it on —
          anyone holding it can knock at the room, and I would rather know who is at the door.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          I record a call only after asking, and an indicator shows on screen whenever a recording is
          running. Recording without every participant agreeing is not something I do, and in several
          states it is not something anyone may do.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Availability</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          I make no promise that this site is always up or always correct. I may change or remove
          anything on it at any time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          To the extent the law allows, I am not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or lost
          profits, arising from your use of this website or the tools on it.
          <strong class="text-ink">This limit applies to the free site only.</strong> Work I am paid
          to do carries its own terms, agreed and signed, and nothing here reduces them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Links out</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Where this site links somewhere else, that place is not mine and I am not responsible for
          what is on it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Which law</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          North Carolina, and the courts sitting in Craven County.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The date at the top changes when this does.
          <a class="link-quiet" href="/privacy/">What the site collects</a> is on its own page.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
